RT-07 follow-up (MG10): no blitter cost for small fills
(build-tree patch, applied after rt07-card-blitter.patch; built as s11rt04).

MG10 measured -rect1 at -20 % on s10rt04 at every -blitmin, rect10 and
the rest within noise: each window fill went through blitFill ->
blitQueue -> blitFlush -> cpuFill, three calls where s8rt04 made one, and
every entry point called blitFlush once more.  The tests are now macros:
BLIT_WANT(w, h) decides before any call, SolidRect draws a fill below the
threshold with its own loop (as it does for pixmaps), and BLIT_FLUSH() is
one compare while the queue is empty.  Rig, s8/s10/s11 (A/B only):
-rect1 111000 / 77500 / 117000 per second.

